    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0230" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/805.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                            Japan to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 18, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In answer to invitation to participate in Chinese loan transmitted in your March
                    11, The Minister for Foreign Affairs expresses appreciation of condition that
                    equal participation be tendered Japan and Russia and undertakes on behalf of his
                    Government to join in said <pb facs="0231" n="115" xml:id="pg115"/> loan,
                    designating the Yokohama Specie Bank as the representative of the Japanese
                    financial group.</p>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs adds: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Imperial Government naturally expect that nothing connected with the
                            projected loan will operate to the prejudice of the special rights and
                            interests of Japan in the region of southern Manchuria.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
